---
name: delegate-context7
description: Delegate tasks requiring external documentation, library code, API references, or SDK searches to an isolated subagent. Prefer delegation over granting MCP access to the current agent to prevent context bloat.
compatibility: opencode
---

## Delegation Policy
Use this skill whenever you need to search or read fresh external documentation or API specs. 
The parent agent MUST NOT request MCP access directly. All interaction must be delegated.

## Execution Rules
1. Delegate this task using OpenCode's `@mention` system (e.g., `@docs-worker` or `@general`).
2. Explicitly instruct the subagent to enable EXACTLY ONE tool: `mcp/context7-mcp`.
3. Pass the payload envelope below to the subagent.

## Subagent Injection Payload
Include this exact structure in your delegation message:

Required Tool: mcp/context7-mcp
Task Prompt: 
"""
ROLE: Specialized Documentation Worker.
TASK: [Insert specific library/API to search and what to extract]

RULES:
1. You may use exactly ONE tool: mcp/context7-mcp.
2. Do not explain your reasoning. Produce only the requested artifact.
3. Maximum response size: 500 tokens, minimal code blocks, concise summary.

OUTPUT FORMAT:
Status: SUCCESS | NOT_FOUND | ERROR
Summary: [Concise technical summary]
References: [Filenames or doc URLs]
Minimal Code: [Only if absolutely necessary]
"""
